<title>USA: Earl Scheib Inc Q2 shr $0.06 vs $0.58.</title>
<headline>Earl Scheib Inc Q2 shr $0.06 vs $0.58.</headline>
<dateline>BEVERLY HILLS, Calif. 1996-12-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>EARL SCHEIB INC.</p>
<p>		 CONDENSED CONSOLIDATED STATEMENTS OF OPERATIONS</p>
<p>			 For the Quarter	 For the Six Months</p>
<p>			    Ended			   Ended</p>
<p>			    Oct. 31,		    Oct. 31,</p>
<p>			  1996	  1995	  1996	  1995</p>
<p> Net sales    $13,290,000 $12,537,000 $27,930,000 $24,673,000</p>
<p>Operating income</p>
<p>			245,000   1,035,000   1,473,000   1,366,000</p>
<p>Income before taxes</p>
<p>			318,000   2,752,000   1,972,000   3,234,000</p>
<p>Income tax expense</p>
<p>			 26,000	95,000	57,000     115,000</p>
<p> Net income	 292,000   2,657,000   1,915,000   3,119,000</p>
<p>Net income per</p>
<p>  share		 6 cts	58 cts	40 cts	68 cts</p>
<p>Weighted average</p>
<p>shares outstanding</p>
<p>		    4,741,000   4,568,000   4,741,000   4,568,000</p>
<p>Note - In last year's second quarter, the company recorded pre-tax income of $1.7 million, $0.37 a share, from the sale of real estate. This year's income from that source was nominal.</p>
<p>The company said operating earnings were impacted primarily by expenses related to tests of image advertising and shop incentive programs that were not productive. These tests have been stopped and the company recently brought it advertising program in-house to improve both its effectiveness and to reduce expenses.</p>
